<title>USA: US Treasury 2-yr notes seen yielding 6.02 pct.</title>
<headline>US Treasury 2-yr notes seen yielding 6.02 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury's auction of $15.5 billion in 2-year notes on Tuesday should produce a yield around 6.02 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>Analysts said with the when-issued yield at least above six percent, the sale could elicit reasonable demand.</p>
<p>Just before the bidding deadline of 1300 EDT/1700 GMT, the 2-year notes were trading with a when-issued yield of 6.02 percent.</p>
<p>Results for the auction are expected around 1345 EDT/1745 GMT.</p>
<p>(( -- North American Treasury Desk, 212-859-1679 ))</p>
